<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maniakh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 568</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maniakh was a Sogdian merchant and diplomat in the service of the Turkic Khaganate. In 568 he led the first Türk embassy to the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justin-ii">Justin II</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, proposing an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> and direct trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> that would bypass <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. His mission, described by the Byzantine historian Menander Protector, opened two decades of Byzantine-Turkic diplomacy.</p></div>
